Y belongs to check applied to x if and only if Y is an O-neighbourhood and either Y equals {0, 1} or x is not bottom. Thus check of bottom is the bottom of O, and check of a non-bottom element is the top of O.

From the relation, a witnessing neighbourhood of x is either the master, which forces Y = {0, 1}, or not the master, which forces x not bottom. Conversely, the master witnesses Y = {0, 1}, and a non-master neighbourhood of a non-bottom x witnesses the other alternative.
